 "result": "The failing call is at `src/tessel/sessions.py:374`, in `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`, where it calls `response.set_cookie(...)`.\n\nThe argument the installed Werkzeug 3.0.3 rejects is `partitioned=partitioned`. The value comes from `self.get_cookie_partitioned(app)` earlier in that method. Werkzeug added the `partitioned` keyword in 3.1, so 3.0.3 raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`.\n\nThe same keyword is also passed to `response.delete_cookie(...)` in the empty-session branch of that method. That path wasn't hit in the failures I saw, but it would presumably fail the same way.",
